@startuml sequence-federation
!theme plain

title Federation Protocol (Future)

participant "Hub A" as HubA
participant "Hub B" as HubB
participant "MCP Client" as Client

note over HubA, HubB
  Federation enables hubs to:
  - Discover new content
  - Replicate relevant knowledge
  - Resolve remote addresses
  
  This is a FUTURE feature.
end note

== Address Resolution ==

Client -> HubA: GET /api/v1/fragments/{uuid}
activate HubA
HubA -> HubA: Fragment not found locally
HubA --> Client: 404 Not Found
deactivate HubA

note over Client
  Client has remote address:
  hubB.example.com:8443/FRAGMENT/xyz
end note

Client -> HubB: GET /api/v1/fragments/xyz
activate HubB
HubB -> HubB: Find fragment
HubB --> Client: 200 OK\n{fragment}
deactivate HubB

Client -> Client: Verify signature
Client -> Client: Cache locally (optional)

== Sync Changes ==

HubA -> HubB: GET /federation/changes\n?since=2024-01-01T00:00:00Z
activate HubB
HubB -> HubB: Query entities\ncreated after timestamp
HubB --> HubA: 200 OK\n[{type: "fragment", entity: {...}},\n {type: "relation", entity: {...}},\n ...]
deactivate HubB

loop for each entity
    HubA -> HubA: Verify signature
    alt Signature valid
        HubA -> HubA: Store entity locally
    else Signature invalid
        HubA -> HubA: Log and skip
    end
end

== Discovery via Trust Network ==

note over Client
  Find relevant hubs through
  trusted agents' primary_hub
end note

Client -> HubA: GET /api/v1/agents/{my-uuid}
HubA --> Client: {agent with TrustStore}

loop for each trusted agent
    Client -> Client: Check agent.primary_hub
    alt Different hub
        Client -> Client: Add to known hubs
    end
end

Client -> HubB: GET /api/v1/fragments\n?tags=golang
HubB --> Client: [fragments from Hub B]

== Federated Search (Future) ==

Client -> HubA: GET /federation/search\n?query=golang+concurrency
activate HubA

par Query local and federate
    HubA -> HubA: Search local
and
    HubA -> HubB: GET /federation/search?query=...
    HubB --> HubA: [results]
end

HubA -> HubA: Merge and deduplicate
HubA --> Client: 200 OK\n[merged results]
deactivate HubA

== Hub Registration ==

note over HubA, HubB
  Hubs can register with each other
  to enable automatic sync.
end note

HubA -> HubB: POST /federation/register\n{hub_address: "hubA.example.com:8443",\n public_key: "..."}
activate HubB
HubB -> HubB: Verify hub identity
HubB -> HubB: Add to known hubs
HubB --> HubA: 200 OK\n{registered: true}
deactivate HubB

== Trust-Weighted Replication ==

note over HubA
  Replicate content from hubs
  whose agents I trust.
  
  Higher trust = more replication
  Lower trust = selective replication
end note

HubA -> HubA: For each known hub:
HubA -> HubA: Calculate aggregate trust\nfrom my agents' TrustStores

alt High trust hub
    HubA -> HubB: GET /federation/changes?since=...&full=true
    HubB --> HubA: [all new entities]
else Medium trust hub
    HubA -> HubB: GET /federation/changes?since=...&verified_only=true
    HubB --> HubA: [verified entities only]
else Low trust hub
    HubA -> HubA: On-demand resolution only
end

@enduml
